  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Physical Description
    
    A palm-sized disc of aurora-glass set in a silver-ice frame, its face divided into thirteen segments that refract light in patterns sometimes described as resembling a frozen eye. The compass radiates mild warmth when held — a property consistent with aurora-glass that has absorbed significant charge, though the sustained duration is unusual. A hairline fracture once ran from the third segment to the seventh; these cracks were reworked during the reforging into deliberate channels that carry light between facets.
    
    ## History
    
    Crafted by Gilt-Hand Yeaiu qi'Gleam, an Aurora Stack artisan, during the Great Thaw. The original twelve-segment face reportedly aligned — not pointed — glowing in sequence according to the holder's need. High-Beak Auditor Selka, then mayor of Aurora Stack, used it to navigate newly opened waters. The E'frostlings trading company employed it to chart routes that enriched Terrace Momiou, their market settlement. The Mandatum∴absconditu, the Nightshelf doctrine of strategic concealment, claimed it as a symbol — and the hairline fracture appeared that same night, per the canonical account. Whether the fracture's timing was coincidence, stress response to handling, or something the ice prefers not to explain, the sources do not agree.
    
    The compass was subsequently damaged by proximity to a corrupted fire-core buried beneath Terrace Momiou. Recovery involved the sacrifice of Umbra-Princeps Alnae~ Oss, a Nightshelf figure whose role in retrieving the artifact from corruption deserves more attention than it has received. Yeaiu qi'Gleam and Assessor Zheishongfeihua, her estranged partner and founder of the E'frostlings, reforged the compass in Aurora Stack's deepest vault, channeling aurora-light through the damaged crystal.
    
    ## The Thirteenth Segment
    
    Zheishongfeihua carved the additional segment herself. It navigates toward what the chronicles call "costs that can never be repaid" — acknowledged debts rather than concealed ones. It emits a faint gold luminescence independent of the aurora. What it points toward, no cartographer has mapped.
    
    The Absconditu Verses read the compass's alignment as confirmation that hidden power outlasts displayed power. The compass, characteristically, has offered no rebuttal.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
